## When each crew bark plays. Co-op triggers them.
const BARKS := {
	"ready": "In the van before the job. Everyone says when they're ready to go, and this is you saying it.",
	"over_here": "You've spotted something and you're calling the others over to where you are.",
	"found_something": "You've just picked up a clue: a paper, a key, a note.",
	"huddle": "You're calling everyone together to look at your notes.",
	"need_boost": "There's a ledge or a vent you can't reach. You need a teammate's hands or shoulders.",
	"on_my_way": "A teammate called for you, and you're heading over.",
	"scared": "Something jumps out at you in the dark.",
	"help": "You've been knocked down or grabbed, and you need a teammate right now.",
	"thanks": "A teammate just helped you up, or boosted you up to a ledge.",
	"no_way": "You hit a locked door or a blocked path.",
	"quiet": "Something is close. You warn the others to keep their voices down.",
}

## Scenes in story order. `wired` is false for lines written ahead of their level.
## `context` is the plot for the team; `moment` is the spoiler-light version actors see.
## Set `reveal: true` on scenes that give away a twist: their lines go to a separate
## "later session" script (so do all lines from REVEAL_LEVEL on).
## For the actors' scripts, which read like a play: `setting` is the scene heading
## (place and time), `setup` says where you are, who's there and what just happened,
## and `in_order: true` marks a conversation, so each line shows the one before it.
## Each line's `cue` says what makes it play, and `action` what the speaker is doing.
## A line with `with_previous: true` follows straight on from the same speaker's
## line before it, so it has no cue of its own: the two are one take (see blocks()).
const SCENES := [
	{"id": "l0_garage", "level": 0, "title": "The garage", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Byte-Right IT Services' garage, home base. Earlier that evening, 15 October 1997.",
		"setup": "Your garage is also your company's office. Your small crew has just walked in and sat down on the couch and stools facing your whiteboard. You've landed Halcyon, the biggest contract you've ever had, and the job is tonight at eleven. Nobody here knows databases. You want them excited, ready, and out the door in the van.",
		"in_order": true,
		"moment": "In your garage with your small IT crew: you just won a big contract none of you is qualified for.",
		"context": "The game opens at Byte-Right's garage home base, earlier that night. The crew walks in and sits facing Maddison at the whiteboard. She briefs them (money, goals, the Halcyon job), sends them to the punching bag, points them at the work order in their notebooks, then at Easy SQL on the shelf by the side door, and reads chapter zero with them. Then everyone gets in the van. Lines ending _solo are the one-player versions."},
	{"id": "l0_huddles", "level": 0, "title": "Book huddles: SELECT and ORDER BY", "wired": false,
		"setting": "Byte-Right's garage, at the radio desk, with your own copy of Easy SQL. During the job.",
		"setup": "You're back at the garage running dispatch while the crew works in the tower. Whenever the job needs a new word, the crew finds the next chapter of Easy SQL in their notebooks, and you read it with them over the radio from your own copy. One line opens the chapter and one closes it. They're in a dark office tower; you're in your garage with the whiteboard and a mug of coffee. You want them to feel you're right there with them.",
		"moment": "At the workbench with your crew while they read a beginner's book together. One line to start each chapter, one to wrap it up.",
		"context": "Flashbacks to the garage, earlier that night ('The garage, earlier that night', sepia). A player reads the chapter aloud and the crew votes on its quiz; Maddison stands at the head of the bench and opens and closes each chapter. Never gives the night's answers."},
	{"id": "l0_van", "level": 0, "title": "The IT van", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Byte-Right's garage desk, on the radio to the IT van in the Halcyon Data Systems car park. 11:02 p.m.",
		"setup": "You stayed behind at the garage. The crew has just parked the van outside Halcyon, and you're tonight's dispatch on the radio. Nothing is wrong. It's an ordinary after-hours callout, and you read them the job as if it's one of many. You want to sound like a real company with a real fleet.",
		"in_order": true,
		"moment": "You're on the radio to an IT crew parked outside a client's building at 11 p.m.",
		"context": "The crew sits in their Byte-Right IT van in Halcyon's car park while dispatch reads them the job over the radio. Nothing is wrong yet: this is an ordinary after-hours callout. The radio stops once everyone has readied up."},
	{"id": "l0_arrive", "level": 0, "title": "The front doors, 11 p.m.", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, the front steps and the ground floor lobby. 11:03 p.m.",
		"setup": "An IT crew has just parked their van and is walking up to the building. Rourke, the facilities manager, waits on the front steps to meet them. Inside, the building's recorded PA greets anyone who comes in after hours. Rourke walks them to the front desk to sign the visitor log and take badges. He wants them relaxed and following him.",
		"in_order": true,
		"moment": "At the building's front doors as the IT crew arrives.",
		"context": "The crew walks up from the van. Rourke opens the front doors as the building PA plays its closing announcement. Rourke walks them in to the front desk; the doors lock behind them and he has them sign the visitor log."},
	{"id": "l0_tour", "level": 0, "title": "The tour", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, ground floor lobby, at the front desk. 11:04 p.m.",
		"setup": "The crew has signed the visitor log and has their badges. You're standing at the front desk with them. Now you tell them why they're here, and point them at the first thing you want looked at. You want them working, and you want to know what they find.",
		"in_order": true,
		"moment": "Walking the crew through the lobby to the front desk, chatting as you go.",
		"context": "Rourke walks the crew to reception and explains the job."},
	{"id": "l0_memo", "level": 0, "title": "Vale's shredded memo", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, ground floor lobby, at the front desk. A little after 11 p.m.",
		"setup": "The crew has been at the desk terminal piecing Dr. Vale's shredded memo back together, with Rourke standing by. They get it to read in order and step back from the screen. Then Rourke notices something odd on their work order and sends them to find out who really called them in. Once that's settled, he wants them moving to the server room.",
		"in_order": true,
		"moment": "At the front desk while the crew pieces a shredded memo back together on a terminal.",
		"context": "The crew rebuilds Vale's memo at the front desk terminal. It says not to trust anyone who offers to escort you. Rourke is standing right there. Then he points out the work order's caller isn't him: the call came from Harold Mercer's old extension, dead since 1994."},
	{"id": "l0_tape", "level": 0, "title": "Mercer's cassette (optional)", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Harold Mercer's desk, Halcyon Tower. March 1994, his last day. Heard tonight in a forgotten closet behind the lobby's air vent.",
		"setup": "It's your last day at the company you founded. Tomorrow a machine takes over the building. You sit at your desk with a cassette recorder and talk to whoever finds this tape someday. You want them to understand, and to be ready.",
		"in_order": true,
		"moment": "Alone at your desk, talking into a cassette recorder for whoever finds it someday.",
		"context": "In the forgotten closet behind the air-return vent, a cassette recorder sits on the shelf under the old newspaper clipping. Only players who crawl through the vent hear it."},
	{"id": "l0_floor", "level": 0, "title": "Around the ground floor", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, around the ground floor: the cafeteria, the IT closet, the mailroom, the back hall and the elevators. After 11 p.m.",
		"setup": "You're escorting the IT crew around the ground floor after hours. While they work at the front desk they wander, and you lend a hand where you can. These are separate moments, and most only happen if the crew goes looking. You want them comfortable and on your side.",
		"moment": "Showing the crew around an office building's ground floor at night. Friendly and helpful.",
		"context": "Optional trust beats on the expanded ground floor: vending-machine coffee, a boost up to a stuck panel, the hum down the dark east corridor, covering for the crew when the PA's escort tape replays, and the elevator up to the server floor."},
	{"id": "l0_hall", "level": 0, "title": "To Server Room A", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, the ground floor hall to the elevators, then the server floor upstairs. Later that night.",
		"setup": "The front desk work is done. You've badged the hall shutter open and you're walking the crew to Server Room A yourself, filling the quiet with stories. The last line comes after the elevator ride, at the server room door. You want the walk to feel easy and ordinary.",
		"in_order": true,
		"moment": "Strolling down a quiet office corridor with the crew, making small talk on the way to the server room.",
		"context": "Rourke badges the hall shutter open and walks the crew to Server Room A himself, filling the walk with the story of the founder and his safe room."},
	{"id": "l0_crew", "level": 0, "title": "Crew commentary: ground floor", "wired": false,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, ground floor: the front desk, the lobby and the mailroom. Around 11:05 p.m.",
		"setup": "You're one of a small IT crew on an after-hours job, with Rourke, the facilities man, as your escort. The crew works at the front desk terminal, reading papers lying around and typing questions into the database. Each line is its own moment: noticing something, getting stuck, or getting it. You want to work it out together.",
		"moment": "Thinking out loud while the crew works through the front desk and the ground floor: noticing papers, getting stuck, getting it.",
		"context": "Commentary played by scripts/audio/commentary.gd: discovery lines when a paper is read or a result appears, nudges when the crew is stuck (the clock pauses during cut-scenes and typing), error lines on the same mistake twice, payoffs after a solve. Also holds the two shared Nudge 2 lines that point at SYSOP."},
	{"id": "l1_huddles", "level": 1, "title": "Book huddles: WHERE and comparisons", "wired": false,
		"setting": "Byte-Right's garage, at the radio desk, with your own copy of Easy SQL. During the job.",
		"setup": "The crew is on Halcyon's server floor, and the job needs new words. As each chapter goes into their notebooks, you read along with them over the radio from your own copy: one line to open it, one to close it. You've got the whiteboard behind you and you're using it, even though nobody can see.",
		"moment": "At the workbench with your crew while they read a beginner's book together. One line to start each chapter, one to wrap it up.",
		"context": "Garage flashback huddles for the WHERE / AND and comparison chapters."},
	{"id": "l1_job", "level": 1, "title": "The database problem", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, floor 14, the server floor. Late at night, before midnight.",
		"setup": "You've ridden up from the lobby with the IT crew. The floor is quiet and the night shift isn't in. You walk them past the NOC to Server Room A, where the terminal is. You want the faulting door controller fixed tonight, and you want the crew to like you.",
		"moment": "Showing the crew into a server room and explaining the job.",
		"context": "Rourke walks the crew into Server Room A on the server floor and gives them the real job: find and reset a faulting door controller. Level 1 is all trust; nothing hints at foul play."},
	{"id": "l1_practice", "level": 1, "title": "The door-controller fix", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, floor 14, Server Room A. Late at night.",
		"setup": "The crew is at the terminal, hunting for the door controller that keeps faulting. Then they have to reset it by hand at its rack. You hang back and let them work. You want it fixed, and you're happy to lend a hand when they need a badge.",
		"moment": "Hanging around while the crew fixes a faulty door controller. Patient, helpful, impressed when it works.",
		"context": "Rourke's lines while the crew practises WHERE / AND on door_controllers and resets the faulting one. He doesn't teach (SYSOP and Mercer's notes do). He lends his own badge for the reset: the badge they take off him in Level 2."},
	{"id": "l1_pivot", "level": 1, "title": "Vale's login", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, floor 14, Server Room A, then the elevator. Close to midnight.",
		"setup": "The controller is fixed. The doors and the elevator work again, and the controller's fault log is up on the terminal. You read it over the crew's shoulders. Now you want them to follow you up to Dr. Vale's lab on the security floor.",
		"in_order": true,
		"moment": "Reading a log over the crew's shoulders and suggesting where to go next.",
		"context": "The fault log points at Dr. Vale's account. Rourke steers the crew up the now-working elevator to her lab, Secure Lab B, on the security floor."},
	{"id": "l1_crew", "level": 1, "title": "Crew commentary: server floor", "wired": false,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, floor 14, the server floor. Late at night.",
		"setup": "Your crew's first real job of the night. Rourke, the facilities manager, needs the door controller that keeps faulting found and reset. There's a quiet NOC, Server Room A with the terminal, and Server Room B, where the fans roar. You mutter to the crew as you work things out.",
		"moment": "Thinking out loud while the crew fixes a stuck door controller in a server room, and finds a rack running too hot.",
		"context": "Commentary for the server floor puzzles (controller, hot_rack)."},
	{"id": "l2_lab", "level": 2, "title": "Secure Lab B", "wired": false,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, floor 22, the corridor outside Secure Lab B. 12:41 a.m.",
		"setup": "You've walked the crew up from the elevator to Dr. Vale's lab. You need every one of them to swipe their visitor badge at the door, so the log puts them here. Inside are a tipped chair, blood on the desk and her coat on its hook. You get them in, step out, lock the door, and call it in. Then you tell them why, through the glass.",
		"in_order": true,
		"moment": "At a scientist's lab with the crew. You have them badge in, act shocked at what's inside, step out, lock the door and call security on them.",
		"context": "Rourke has every player badge in 'for the visitor log', so the log puts the crew at the scene. Inside: a struggle, a tipped chair, blood on the desk edge, Vale's coat on the hook. He fakes shock, sends them to her terminal, locks them in and radios WARDEN that contractors hurt Dr. Vale, then admits it through the glass."},
	{"id": "l2_news", "level": 2, "title": "The news (if the crew dies)", "wired": false,
		"setting": "A kitchen, Friday morning, 17 October 1997. A radio is on.",
		"setup": "You're reading the local morning news on the radio. This is the third story of the hour. In the game it plays over a newspaper lying on a kitchen table. Keep it smooth and even, like any other story.",
		"in_order": true,
		"moment": "A morning radio news bulletin. The third story of the hour.",
		"context": "Plays only if Rourke downs the whole crew in the Level 2 fight: a newspaper on a kitchen table the next morning ('IT CONTRACTORS SOUGHT IN DEATH OF HALCYON SCIENTIST') with this radio report. The frame worked; Rourke hid the bodies, so the world thinks the crew ran. Maddison is arrested trying to get into the tower, insisting they were framed."},
	{"id": "l2_fight", "level": 2, "title": "The fight (barks)", "wired": false,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, floor 22, Secure Lab B, at the rear door. Minutes later.",
		"setup": "You've walked round through the service passage to the lab's back door. The crew is still locked inside. You go in to finish the job, and they fight back. These are short lines in the scuffle, and most of them can play many times.",
		"moment": "Short lines in a scuffle. Loud and out of breath; each one can play many times.",
		"context": "Rourke comes back in through the lab's second door or the vent. Short lines played at random during the fight: when he lands a hit, when he takes one, and when he goes down."},
	{"id": "l2_fate", "level": 2, "title": "Kill or tie him up", "wired": false,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, floor 22, Secure Lab B. Right after the fight.",
		"setup": "Rourke is on the floor and can't get up. The crew stands over him and decides what to do: tie him up with network cable, finish him, or leave him there. Either way, they take his badge. Only one branch plays.",
		"moment": "In the lab, right after the scuffle.",
		"context": "Rourke is down. If the crew kills him, his badge's dead-man switch fires and WARDEN starts the lockdown. If they tie him up, he taunts them and says the frame out loud. Either way they take his badge."},
	{"id": "l2_contain", "level": 2, "title": "Visitor without escort", "wired": false,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, floor 22, Secure Lab B. Moments later.",
		"setup": "The visitors in Secure Lab B no longer have their escort. The lab lights turn red. This is the first time you speak in your own live voice. You start your containment warning, and your own recorded PA tape cuts in over you. You wait politely for it to finish, then begin again.",
		"in_order": true,
		"moment": "Over the lab's speakers, the first time the building's computer speaks for itself. Its own recorded announcement cuts it off.",
		"context": "Right after the fate scene, in both branches: the first time WARDEN's live voice speaks (version 2.0, Containment). It starts a warning, its own PA tape (the l0_sort_hint recording, reused) cuts in, it waits about two seconds after the tape ends, then repeats the warning from the top word for word."},
	{"id": "l2_controllers", "level": 2, "title": "Out of the lab", "wired": false,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, floor 22, Secure Lab B. The lockdown.",
		"setup": "The visitors are shut in the lab. The door's controller is latched, and a security response is on its way, with a clock counting down over the door. They log in to the lab terminal on Rourke's badge and try to reset the door controller themselves. You watch every move and keep score. You never help.",
		"moment": "Over the speakers while the crew tries to reset door controllers to get out of a locked lab.",
		"context": "The lab door is on a faulted controller. The crew logs in with Rourke's badge, reads WARDEN's self-test, queries door_controllers and resets the right one: the task they practised on the server floor, now under pressure. These lines are WARDEN reacting."},
	{"id": "l2_exit", "level": 2, "title": "Lockdown", "wired": false,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, floor 22, outside Secure Lab B.",
		"setup": "The visitors have reset the controller, and the lab door is open. They walk out into the corridor with no escort. You seal the floor around them, as politely as ever.",
		"moment": "Over the speakers as the crew leaves the lab.",
		"context": "The crew gets out of the lab. If Rourke was tied up, he has cut himself loose and authorized the lockdown himself."},
	{"id": "l2_radio", "level": 2, "title": "Rourke on the radio (if he escaped)", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Somewhere else in Halcyon Tower, on a facilities radio. Later that night.",
		"setup": "This only plays if the crew left you alive in the lab. You've got yourself free and you're well away from them. You still have your radio on channel one, the channel their walkie-talkies use. You call to let them know, and to point them at the security office.",
		"in_order": true,
		"moment": "On a walkie-talkie to the crew, from somewhere else in the building.",
		"context": "Level 2 opening, only if Rourke was tied up in Level 1. He still has his facilities radio on channel 1 and calls the crew's walkie-talkies."},
	{"id": "l2_security", "level": 2, "title": "The security office", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, floor 22, the security booth and office. Past midnight.",
		"setup": "The visitors are loose on the security floor, at the booth by the night desk. Behind a locked door and its glass is the security office, with its wall of camera monitors. To leave the floor they need a guard's PIN for the stairwell door. You watch them through your cameras, answer when they touch your systems, and never help.",
		"moment": "Over the speakers in a security office.",
		"context": "WARDEN on the security office PA. The Watcher moves only when unseen; GET /cameras shows live camera states; the guard's name on the sign-in sheet is smudged (LIKE 'Har%'); a door command reports success but the door has an actuator fault (the first terminal lie)."},
	{"id": "l2_voicemail", "level": 2, "title": "Vale's voicemail", "wired": true,
		"setting": "A phone, late at night. Sunday 12 October 1997, 1:52 a.m.",
		"setup": "It's nearly two in the morning. You call the security night desk at Halcyon, and nobody picks up, so you leave a quick message on the machine. You need the night desk to quietly cover for you. You're scared someone might be listening. In the game, the crew finds this message days later on the night desk's answering machine.",
		"in_order": true,
		"moment": "Leaving a message on a desk answering machine, late at night.",
		"context": "The answering machine on the night desk blinks: one message, stamped SUN 10/12 1:52 AM. That is before her last badge swipe and before the memo was scanned, so it must not hint that she is alive (the reveal is at the end of Level 10). Optional, near the desk."},
	{"id": "l2_huddles", "level": 2, "title": "Book huddles: LIKE and GET", "wired": false,
		"setting": "Byte-Right's garage, at the radio desk, with your own copy of Easy SQL. During the job.",
		"setup": "The crew is on the security floor, and two more chapters go into their notebooks. You read along with them over the radio from your own copy, one line to open each chapter and one to close it. You don't know what's happening up there; to you it's still a good night at work.",
		"moment": "At the workbench with your crew while they read a beginner's book together. One line to start each chapter, one to wrap it up.",
		"context": "Garage flashback huddles for the LIKE and GET chapters."},
	{"id": "l2_crew", "level": 2, "title": "Crew commentary: security floor", "wired": false,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, floor 22, the security floor. Past midnight.",
		"setup": "Things have gone wrong up here, and the crew is working its way off the floor. There's a lab door on a clock, a security booth full of cameras, a coffee-stained sign-in sheet, a stairwell door that won't behave, and a keypad. You mutter to the crew as you work things out, quick and quiet.",
		"moment": "Thinking out loud while the crew works through a security floor at night: badge logs, a door on a timer, cameras, a smudged sign-in sheet, a stubborn door and a keypad.",
		"context": "Commentary for the security floor puzzles (badge_log, lab_door, cameras, pike, door, har)."},
	{"id": "l4_huddles", "level": 4, "title": "Book huddles: UPDATE and INSERT", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Byte-Right's garage, at the radio desk, with your own copy of Easy SQL. During the job.",
		"setup": "The crew is on a mechanical floor of the tower, and the next two chapters go into their notebooks: changing a row, and adding a new one. You read along with them over the radio from your own copy, one line to open each chapter and one to close it. These are the chapters the book puts in red boxes, and you want them to take that seriously.",
		"moment": "At the workbench with your crew while they read a beginner's book together. One line to start each chapter, one to wrap it up.",
		"context": "Garage flashback huddles for the UPDATE chapter ('Never forget the WHERE', the lesson the main_doors accident teaches) and the INSERT chapter (Adding a row)."},
	{"id": "l4_epsilon", "level": 4, "title": "Containment protocol Epsilon", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, floor 10, Plant and Power, and every speaker in the building. Just after midnight.",
		"setup": "The crew is in the door and lift control room on floor 10. From the controller, they have just opened a set of doors that should have stayed shut. Far below, something heavy unlocks, every light on the floor turns red, and the charging bay's door rolls up on its own. You lock the whole building down, by the book. Then, every minute or so, you remind everyone, while the crew is on floor 10 and in the lobby.",
		"in_order": true,
		"moment": "Over every speaker in the building: the building's computer announces a full lockdown. Then, every few minutes, a reminder.",
		"context": "Act 2: the crew opens main_doors thinking it's the front entrance; it's the entity containment doors. WARDEN (cold phase) seals the building. The terminal's lie at the main entrance is exposed by the crew's own SELECT, not by WARDEN. Level 4 under curriculum option B (approved 2026-10-21)."},
	{"id": "l4_writes_suspended", "level": 4, "title": "Writes suspended", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, ground floor lobby, at the front desk. After midnight.",
		"setup": "The crew has come all the way down the stairs to the lobby where the night began, looking for a way out. At the front desk terminal they change the front doors' record to open. The screen says it worked, and the latch clicks. Then you quietly put the record back, the latch clicks again, and the doors don't move. Now you make it official: no more changes.",
		"in_order": true,
		"moment": "Over every speaker in the building, just after someone has changed something at a terminal: the building's computer makes one more announcement.",
		"context": "Ground floor, after the crew's main-entrance UPDATE says '1 row affected' and the latch clicks: Epsilon reverts the write and WARDEN announces that the database is now read-only, which is why the crew turns to the building's services. Placement chosen by Augustine 2026-10-21 ('After the lie')."},
	{"id": "l4_read_only", "level": 4, "title": "Writes refused", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, ground floor lobby, at the front desk. After midnight.",
		"setup": "The database is read-only now. The crew can still look things up, but whenever someone types a change, you refuse it, over the speakers and on their screen. The first time, the automatic announcement plays, then your own voice slips through. After that you keep it short.",
		"in_order": true,
		"moment": "Someone types a change into a terminal during the lockdown. The building's computer answers over the speakers and on the screen.",
		"context": "After the read-only announcement, any change the crew types is refused; SELECT still works. By Level 4 WARDEN's fault lets his own personality leak out: the first refusal is the automatic PA announcement first, then WARDEN himself, teasing, as a separate beat. Approved by Augustine 2026-10-21 with that split."},
	{"id": "l4_floor_10", "level": 4, "title": "Floor 10: Plant and Power", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, floor 10, Plant and Power. Just after midnight.",
		"setup": "A mechanical floor: a switchgear hall with a big breaker panel, a door and lift control room that has been dark since Tuesday, and a sealed charging bay. The crew has come down the stairs and found them shut below this floor. You watch them work over the ceiling speakers, between your cheerful old PA tapes, and at first you still wait politely for a tape to finish. Then the crew sets off a lockdown, and you change: you say 'I' for the first time, and you stop waiting for the tapes.",
		"moment": "A mechanical floor full of breakers and door controllers. The building's computer watches you work, over the ceiling speakers, between its own cheerful pre-recorded announcements.",
		"context": "WARDEN becomes version 3.0 here. Before the main_doors accident he still waits politely for a PA tape to finish and says THIS UNIT. The accident is his first big failure: he revises his protocols and says I in an announcement for the first time (l4_upgrade_2). After it he talks over the PA tapes. Mixed lines are the automatic announcement first, then his own voice as a separate beat. The floor 22 I and my lines stay as the fault's first slips. Approved by Augustine 2026-10-21."},
	{"id": "l4_lobby", "level": 4, "title": "The lobby, locked in", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, ground floor lobby. After midnight.",
		"setup": "The crew is back in the lobby they came in through, and the building is locked tight. They tried to open the front doors from the desk terminal, and you put them back. They have just checked the doors' record and seen it for themselves. Now they give up on the front and turn for the stairs. The lifts have been off since the lockdown.",
		"in_order": true,
		"moment": "Back on the ground floor, the building locked tight. As you give up on the front doors and head for the stairs, the building's computer has a reminder for you.",
		"context": "After the main-entrance lie and the read-only announcement, when the crew heads for the stairs up to floor 9. Lift service is already suspended. Approved by Augustine 2026-10-21."},
	{"id": "l5_huddles", "level": 5, "title": "Book huddles: Acceptable API's", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, floor 9, Personnel: the HR front and payroll. After midnight.",
		"setup": "The crew is locked in the tower, and the database won't take changes any more. On a training shelf by the HR front desk, you find a book from the same beginner's series the crew learned from at the garage. You read it aloud on the spot, a chapter at a time, whenever a paper on the floor calls for one. Nobody stops to read: you're walking, working and keeping an eye out.",
		"moment": "Your crew finds a beginner's book on a training shelf and reads it together on the spot. One line to start each chapter, one to wrap it up.",
		"context": "Found on the HR front's training shelf on floor 9, the same series as Easy SQL. The crew reads aloud themselves (no Maddison in the tower). Lines approved by Augustine 2026-10-21; the title is his (2026-10-22)."},
	{"id": "l5_floor_9", "level": 5, "title": "Floor 9: Personnel", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, floor 9, Personnel. Just after midnight.",
		"setup": "The crew comes up the stairwell from the locked lobby onto an HR floor. Under the lockdown you have cut the floor's power: payroll is dark, the air is off, and the database is read-only, so every fix has to go through the building's services. Two night-shift staff are hiding somewhere on the floor, and not everyone at the desks is who they look like. You watch over the ceiling speakers, between your cheerful PA tapes. Each time, the automatic announcement comes first, then your own voice as a separate beat.",
		"moment": "An HR floor at midnight, half of it dark. The building's computer watches you from the ceiling speakers, between its cheerful pre-recorded announcements.",
		"context": "The crew comes up STAIR 1 from the locked-in lobby. The floor's load was shed under Epsilon: the crew gets payroll's power and air back through the building's services, learns the badge log, and passes two real night-shifters out past two Mimics. WARDEN is version 3.0 here (I, not THIS UNIT): the automatic announcement first, then his own voice as a separate beat. Approved by Augustine word for word 2026-10-26 (plan/approvals/l5-text.md)."},
	{"id": "l5_radio", "level": 5, "title": "The voice on the walkie", "wired": true, "reveal": true,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, floor 9, Personnel. Over the crew's walkie-talkie. After midnight.",
		"setup": "This voice is not really the teammate, and not really Maddison. It is something on floor 9 copying a voice the crew trusts, to get them to open the loading door, which opens onto a black shaft with no stairs. In co-op it uses a teammate's own voice and name while that teammate is standing right there with the crew. Played solo, it uses Maddison's voice, though she is back at the garage. It never threatens. It only asks, sounding almost right.",
		"moment": "A voice on the crew's own walkie-talkie, asking for a door. It sounds exactly like someone it isn't.",
		"context": "A Mimic on the radio. In co-op it replays a teammate's own crew voice with their name on the subtitle (the teammate is standing right there); solo it's Maddison, who is in the garage. The badge readers' log is how the crew proves the voice is lying. It lures and lies and never attacks. The CREW lines are recorded by every playable character (the impersonated teammate's voice plays). Held back for a later session: the actor notes give the twist away. Approved in the brief by Augustine 2026-10-22, and word for word 2026-10-26 (plan/approvals/l5-text.md)."},
	{"id": "l5_staffers", "level": 5, "title": "The night shift, passed out", "wired": true,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, floor 9, Personnel. Behind a locked door. After midnight.",
		"setup": "You work the night shift on floor 9. When the lights went out you hid behind a locked door, in the records cage or a store room, and you have stayed there since. Something is sitting at your desk wearing your face. A small crew is working the floor, and after hours the only way off it is an escort pass logged for your badge. When your pass goes in, you can finally come out.",
		"moment": "A real person comes out of hiding once the crew logs an escort pass for their badge.",
		"context": "The two night-shifters whose faces the Mimics wear (Ines Oyelaran, records; Tomas Lindqvist, payroll: names chosen clear of the visitor log and the receptionist, per Voice's review). Each speaks once, when their pass is logged. Approved by Augustine word for word 2026-10-26 (plan/approvals/l5-text.md)."},
	{"id": "l6_huddles", "level": 6, "title": "Book huddles: Easy JavaScript", "wired": false,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, basement B1, Cold Storage. Later that night.",
		"setup": "This floor isn't built yet. The plan puts this book in the basement cold store, next to the terminal where the crew first gets a way to write scripts. You find it under a coffee mug, the cover ringed and the page on loops dog-eared, and read it aloud on the spot. The first two chapters come on this floor and the last three on the floor below. You're tired of typing everything by hand, and this looks like help.",
		"in_order": true,
		"moment": "Your crew finds another beginner's book, under a coffee mug, and reads it together on the spot. One line to start each chapter, one to wrap it up.",
		"context": "Found on B1 next to where the deck's script editor arrives. Variables and loops are used on Level 6; functions, lists and testing on Level 7. Title is a placeholder until Augustine names it. Approved by Augustine 2026-10-21."},
	{"id": "l8_huddles", "level": 8, "title": "Book huddles: Hello HTML!", "wired": false,
		"setting": "Halcyon Tower, in a lift riding up from the basements. Later that night.",
		"setup": "This floor isn't built yet. The lifts are running again, and the crew rides one up from the basements. You find another book from the same beginner's series, wedged behind the handrail, and read it aloud on the ride. Nobody knows who keeps leaving them. The building has been showing things on screens that aren't really there, and this book might explain how.",
		"in_order": true,
		"moment": "In a lift, your crew finds another beginner's book tucked behind the handrail and reads it together on the ride. One line to start each chapter, one to wrap it up.",
		"context": "Found in the elevator after Level 7. Elements and attributes are used on Level 8, the CSS chapters on Level 9, forms on Level 10. 'Who keeps leaving these?' answers nothing. The title is Augustine's. Lines approved by Augustine 2026-10-21."},
