		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Thumbing over his shoulder at the lost and found behind the desk."},
	"l0_memo_3": {"scene": "l0_memo", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "And yes, you hop the counter. Company's big on fitness, so there's no gate. Means nobody sneaks back there either.",
		"note": "Amused, he's said this to every visitor. A little eye-roll at corporate.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Patting the top of the counter with his palm."},
	"l0_memo_4": {"scene": "l0_memo", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Grab one and I'll take you to the server room.",
		"note": "Friendly.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Turning toward the hall, already a step away."},
	"l0_walkie": {"scene": "l0_memo", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Channel one. Keep them on. Reception's lousy once we're past the shutter. This way.",
		"note": "Offhand.",
		"cue": "Just after you've covered for the crew with the PA, as you lead them toward the hall.",
		"action": "Walking off toward the hall, waving them after him.",
		"jot": "Walkies on channel one."},
	"l0_tape_1": {"scene": "l0_tape", "speaker": "MERCER", "text": "Harold Mercer. March of '94. My last day, apparently.",
		"note": "Dry.",
		"cue": "Only if a player crawls through the lobby's air vent into a forgotten closet and presses play on the cassette on the shelf.",
		"action": "Clicking record on the cassette recorder, then leaning in."},
	"l0_tape_2": {"scene": "l0_tape", "speaker": "MERCER", "text": "If you're hearing this, you crawled through a vent to get in here. Good. You don't trust doors.",
		"note": "Approving, a little smile.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Sitting back in his chair, recorder in hand."},
	"l0_tape_3": {"scene": "l0_tape", "speaker": "MERCER", "text": "Tomorrow a machine runs the locks, the lights and the air. I told the board you don't hand the keys to something that can't be locked out.",
		"note": "The one moment of anger, still controlled.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Gripping the edge of his desk."},
	"l0_tape_4": {"scene": "l0_tape", "speaker": "MERCER", "text": "So I've drawn up a room it can't get into. No wires in, no wires out. Whether I ever get to build it is another matter.",
		"note": "Quiet, almost proud, then wry on the last sentence.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Glancing down at drawings spread across his desk.",
		"secret": true},
	"l0_tape_5": {"scene": "l0_tape", "speaker": "MERCER", "text": "If it ever comes to that, look for my plans. The building's records remember more than people do.",
		"note": "Slow.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "The end of the tape. Leaning close to the recorder, then clicking stop.",
		"secret": true},
	"l0_sra": {"scene": "l0_hall", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Here we are. Server Room A.",
		"note": "Pleasant, like the end of a tour.",
		"cue": "Upstairs on the server floor, after the elevator ride. You've led the crew past the operations room window to the server room door.",
		"action": "Swiping his badge at the server room door."},

	# --- Level 1 -------------------------------------------------------------
	"l0_coffee": {"scene": "l0_floor", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Machine's been eating quarters since '94. Watch. ... There. Coffee's on me. Don't tell facilities.",
		"note": "Proud of the trick.",
		"cue": "Only if a player tries the cafeteria vending machine while you're free. It eats their quarter, and you come over to help. Once a night.",
		"action": "Thumping the side of the vending machine until a cup drops."},
	"l0_boost_1": {"scene": "l0_floor", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Panel's stuck up top? Here, step on my hands. I've got you.",
		"note": "Easy, practised.",
		"cue": "Only if a player tries the stuck ceiling panel in the IT closet while you're free. You come over to help. Once a night.",
		"action": "Lacing his fingers together, crouching for a boost."},
	"l0_boost_2": {"scene": "l0_floor", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "See? Teamwork.",
		"note": "Brushing his hands off.",
		"cue": "Right after the player shoves the panel up and an old sticker drops out of the ceiling.",
		"action": "Brushing his hands off, stepping back."},
	"l0_hum": {"scene": "l0_floor", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Don't mind the hum down that way. Old transformer. There's been a ticket open on it since before my time.",
		"note": "Near the dark east corridor. Casual, but he doesn't look down it.",
		"cue": "Walking the crew down the hall, right after the founder story, as you pass the dark passage to the east corridor.",
		"action": "Strolling on past the dark passage, waving a hand at it."},
	"l0_cover": {"scene": "l0_floor", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "They're with me. Escort's right here.",
		"note": "Covering for them like a friend.",
		"cue": "The crew is around the counter getting walkie-talkies when the PA's escort announcement plays again.",
		"action": "Looking up at the ceiling speaker, one hand raised."},
	"l0_elevator": {"scene": "l0_floor", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Server floor's up on fourteen. Elevator's slow, but it gets there.",
		"note": "At the elevator bank, holding the door.",
		"cue": "You've walked the crew to the end of the hall and opened the door to the elevators.",
		"action": "Holding the door open, waving the crew past him.",
		"jot": "Server floor is up on fourteen."},
	"l0_lift_button": {"scene": "l0_floor", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Press fourteen for me, would you? Server floor.",
		"note": "Easy, polite.",
		"cue": "Inside the elevator, once you've stepped in ahead of the crew.",
		"action": "Leaning on the back wall of the car, across from the buttons."},
	"cc_nudge2_first": {"scene": "l0_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "That SYSOP on the screen seems to know this building. Maybe ask.",
		"note": "Stuck, before SYSOP has helped. Half a joke, half serious.",
		"cue": "Only when the crew has been stuck on a puzzle for a couple of minutes, or has failed twice. This version plays the first time, on any floor, before that name on the screen has helped you.",
		"action": "Staring at the terminal screen, half smiling."},
	"cc_nudge2": {"scene": "l0_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Whoever SYSOP is, they've been right so far. Maybe ask.",
		"note": "Stuck again. A little uneasy about trusting a stranger on a screen.",
		"cue": "The same kind of moment, any time later, once that name on the screen has already helped you.",
		"action": "Frowning at the screen, arms folded."},
	"l0_cc_peek_card": {"scene": "l0_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Quick-start card for the scanner. Somebody's filled in the blanks.",
		"note": "Picked up a scanner's instruction card. Noticing handwriting on it.",
		"cue": "A player picks up the scanner's quick-start card on the front desk and reads it.",
		"action": "Holding the little card up, squinting at the handwriting."},
	"l0_cc_peek_n1a": {"scene": "l0_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Scanners always come with instructions. Check round the keyboard.",
		"note": "Stuck for a minute. A practical thought.",
		"cue": "Only if the crew has been stuck for about a minute finding where the scans went, and nobody has read the scanner card yet.",
		"action": "Leaning over the front desk, glancing around the keyboard."},
	"l0_cc_peek_n1b": {"scene": "l0_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "That scanner card had something written in by hand.",
		"note": "Stuck. Remembering the card you all read.",
		"cue": "The same stuck moment, but the crew has already read the scanner card.",
		"action": "Tapping the desk beside the keyboard, thinking."},
	"l0_cc_peek_err": {"scene": "l0_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Is that what the card called it?",
		"note": "The same name typed wrong twice. Gentle doubt.",
		"cue": "Only if someone types the same wrong name twice.",
		"action": "Looking over a teammate's shoulder at the terminal."},
	"l0_cc_peek_pay": {"scene": "l0_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Scraps of a memo. All jumbled up.",
		"note": "Seeing the result. Curious.",
		"cue": "The scraps come up on the terminal screen for the first time.",
		"action": "Leaning in toward the screen."},
	"l0_cc_memo_disc": {"scene": "l0_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Every scrap's got a number. That's not an accident.",
		"note": "Spotting a pattern in the jumbled scraps.",
		"cue": "While the jumbled scraps are up on the screen.",
		"action": "Running a finger down the screen."},
	"l0_cc_memo_n1a": {"scene": "l0_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Didn't the scanner come with a card? It might say how the scraps are kept.",
		"note": "Stuck. Thinking back.",
		"cue": "Only if the crew has been stuck for about a minute putting the scraps in order, and nobody has read the scanner card yet.",
		"action": "Chewing a thumbnail, looking around the desk."},
	"l0_cc_memo_n1b": {"scene": "l0_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "The scanner card said something about numbering the scraps.",
		"note": "Stuck. Remembering the card.",
		"cue": "The same stuck moment, but the crew has already read the scanner card.",
		"action": "Glancing at the scanner card on the desk."},
	"l0_cc_memo_back": {"scene": "l0_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "It reads backwards. We've got the ending first.",
		"note": "The memo came out in reverse, twice. Amused.",
		"cue": "Only if the crew sorts the memo and it comes out backwards, twice.",
		"action": "Tilting their head at the screen, grinning."},
	"l0_cc_memo_pay": {"scene": "l0_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "...Don't look at him. Just don't look at him.",
		"note": "Whispered. The memo warns about the man standing right next to you.",
		"cue": "The memo finally reads in order on the screen, and Rourke is standing right beside you.",
		"action": "Eyes fixed on the screen, barely moving their lips."},
	"l0_cc_caller_order": {"scene": "l0_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Work order's got a callback extension on it.",
		"note": "Reading the work order. Noticing a detail.",
		"cue": "A player reads the work order in their notebook.",
		"action": "Holding the open notebook, finger on the work order."},
	"l0_cc_caller_list": {"scene": "l0_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "A phone list. With extensions.",
		"note": "Finding a staff phone list.",
		"cue": "A player finds and reads the staff phone list pinned up in the mailroom.",
		"action": "Standing at the mailroom wall, reading the pinned-up list."},
	"l0_cc_caller_n1a": {"scene": "l0_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Rourke said the mailroom has the only phone list that's right.",
		"note": "Stuck. Remembering what the escort said.",
		"cue": "Only if the crew has been stuck for about a minute on who called, and nobody has read the mailroom's phone list.",
		"action": "Turning to look down the back corridor."},
	"l0_cc_caller_n1b": {"scene": "l0_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "That phone list in the mailroom had everybody's extension.",
		"note": "Stuck. Remembering the list.",
		"cue": "The same stuck moment, but the crew has already read the mailroom's phone list.",
		"action": "Flipping back through the notebook, thinking."},
	"l0_cc_caller_err": {"scene": "l0_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Is that what the column's actually called?",
		"note": "The same column name wrong twice. Gentle doubt.",
		"cue": "Only if someone gets the same column name wrong twice.",
		"action": "Looking over a teammate's shoulder at the terminal."},
	"l0_cc_caller_pay": {"scene": "l0_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "So that's who called us. Weird.",
		"note": "Uneasy. That isn't who you expected.",
		"cue": "The crew finds the name behind the work order's phone extension.",
		"action": "Sitting back from the screen, frowning."},
	"l0_cc_book_disc": {"scene": "l0_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Last page is torn out. Somebody didn't want their name in here.",
		"note": "Reading a visitor book. Suspicious.",
		"cue": "Only if a player picks up the visitor book on the front desk and reads it.",
		"action": "Flipping to the back of the visitor book."},
	"l0_cc_book_n1": {"scene": "l0_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "The book's only paper. The front desk computer might keep its own copy.",
		"note": "Stuck. A practical idea.",
		"cue": "Only if the crew is stuck on the visitor book after reading it.",
		"action": "Setting the book down, nodding at the terminal."},
	"l0_cc_book_pay": {"scene": "l0_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Vale signed in. And never signed out.",
		"note": "Quietly. That's not good.",
		"cue": "The front desk computer's sign-in list shows the last name before yours.",
		"action": "Staring at the screen, voice dropping."},
	"l1_huddle_where_1": {"scene": "l1_huddles", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "WHERE. For finding one thing in a big pile. Like my car keys.",
		"note": "Patting pockets.",
		"cue": "On the server floor, the chapter 'Keeping only some rows' goes into the crew's notebooks. You open it.",
		"action": "At the radio desk, the open book in one hand."},
	"l1_huddle_where_2": {"scene": "l1_huddles", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Two conditions, you glue them together with AND. Both have to be true. Like payday AND the cheque clears.",
		"note": "Rueful.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Holding up two fingers, then pressing them together."},
	"l1_huddle_compare_1": {"scene": "l1_huddles", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Bigger than, smaller than. The little alligator signs. Mouth eats the bigger number.",
		"note": "Drawing one on the whiteboard, with teeth.",
		"cue": "Optional. Only if the crew goes after the overheating rack: the chapter 'More than, less than' goes into their notebooks.",
		"action": "Uncapping a marker and turning to the whiteboard behind you."},
	"l1_huddle_compare_2": {"scene": "l1_huddles", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Okay. That's maths I actually remember from school.",
		"note": "Relieved.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Capping the marker and stepping back from the board."},
	"l1_enter": {"scene": "l1_job", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "In you come. Terminal's just over here.",
		"note": "Calling back over his shoulder, inside the room.",
		"cue": "You've just reached Server Room A's door. You lead the crew inside.",
		"action": "Leading them in, heading for the terminal desk."},
	"l1_terminal": {"scene": "l1_job", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Here's our database problem. One of the door controllers on this floor keeps faulting, and half the doors up here won't open till it's reset. Hopefully it's a quick fix.",
		"note": "Mundane, a facilities guy with a real problem. Hopeful.",
		"cue": "You've reached the terminal desk, and the crew has caught up with you.",
		"action": "Standing by the terminal desk, turning to whoever is closest."},
	"l1_noc_1": {"scene": "l1_job", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "That's the NOC. Network operations. Night shift logs everything in there. Every alarm, every coffee break.",
		"note": "Easy, tour-guide tone.",
		"cue": "The first line on this floor. The crew steps off the elevator behind you, and you pass the NOC's window.",
		"action": "Walking ahead down the corridor, nodding at the NOC window."},
	"l1_noc_2": {"scene": "l1_job", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Night shift's not in tonight. Their log's still on the desk, though. They write it all down, whether anyone reads it or not.",
		"note": "Only if a player goes into the NOC. Leaning in the doorway.",
		"cue": "Optional. Only if a player wanders into the NOC. Plays once.",
		"action": "Following them over, glancing at the log on the desk.",
		"jot": "Rourke said the night shift writes every alarm down. Their log's still on this floor somewhere.", "case": "controller", "found_in": ["NOC SHIFT LOG"]},
	"l1_waiting": {"scene": "l1_practice", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Take your time. I've been staring at that rack for a week.",
		"note": "Patient.",
		"cue": "About a minute after you hand the crew the job, if they still haven't found the controller.",
		"action": "Leaning on the doorframe, arms folded, watching them work."},
	"l1_badge_help": {"scene": "l1_practice", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Reset wants a badge? Here, use mine.",
		"note": "Helpful, no hesitation.",
		"cue": "The crew finds the right rack and tries its reset. You walk over to it.",
		"action": "Walking to the rack and swiping your own badge."},
	"l1_wrong_panel": {"scene": "l1_practice", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Nope, panel's not having it. Try another?",
		"note": "No blame.",
		"cue": "Each time a player tries the reset on the wrong rack. Can repeat.",
		"action": "Watching from across the room, shrugging."},
	"l1_fixed_1": {"scene": "l1_practice", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Would you look at that. Green across the board. Six months I've been filing tickets on that thing.",
		"note": "Genuinely impressed.",
		"cue": "Right after your badge goes through. The rack reads OK, and the stuck doors and the elevator come back.",
		"action": "Stepping back from the rack, staring at it."},
	"l1_fixed_2": {"scene": "l1_practice", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "You lot are good. Director's going to want to hear about this.",
		"note": "Warm. On a replay, the director hearing about them is the problem.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Turning to the crew with a grin."},
	"l1_pivot_1": {"scene": "l1_pivot", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Hang on. That fault log... every reset this week came from Vale's login.",
		"note": "Curious, a little too quickly.",
		"cue": "Straight after you praise the crew. The controller's fault log comes up on the terminal.",
		"action": "Leaning over a teammate's shoulder, reading the screen."},
	"l1_pivot_2": {"scene": "l1_pivot", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Her lab's up on the security floor. Secure Lab B.",
		"note": "Thinking out loud.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Straightening up, eyes still on the screen."},
	"l1_pivot_3": {"scene": "l1_pivot", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Come on. If anyone can tell us what she was up to, it's her own terminal. Elevator works now, thanks to you.",
		"note": "Friendly, steering.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Heading for the door, waving them along."},
	"l1_lift_button": {"scene": "l1_pivot", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Twenty-two. Security floor. Go on.",
		"note": "A little clipped now, eager to get there.",
		"cue": "The whole crew has caught up with you at the elevator, and you've stepped into the car.",
		"action": "Standing in the car, across from the buttons, nodding at them."},
	"l1_cc_log": {"scene": "l1_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Night shift wrote down every alarm. That has to help.",
		"note": "Reading a shift log. Encouraged.",
		"cue": "The first time a player reads the night shift's log in the NOC.",
		"action": "Holding up the shift log, running a finger down it."},
	"l1_cc_sheet": {"scene": "l1_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "There's a sheet on the controllers in here. Hang on to that.",
		"note": "Finding a reference sheet. Pleased.",
		"cue": "The first time a player reads the door controller sheet on Server Room A's terminal desk.",
		"action": "Picking the sheet up off the terminal desk."},
	"l1_cc_nudge1_a": {"scene": "l1_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Rourke said the night shift logs everything. Maybe they saw this happen.",
		"note": "Stuck for a minute. Remembering what the escort said.",
		"cue": "After the crew has been stuck finding the faulty controller for about a minute, if nobody has read the night shift's log yet.",
		"action": "Leaning back from the terminal, looking toward the NOC."},
	"l1_cc_nudge1_b": {"scene": "l1_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "What did that shift log say the alarms were about?",
		"note": "Stuck. Thinking back to the log.",
		"cue": "Same moment, stuck for about a minute, but someone has already read the shift log.",
		"action": "Drumming your fingers beside the terminal."},
	"l1_cc_err_table": {"scene": "l1_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Is that what the sheet in here called it?",
		"note": "The same table name wrong twice. Gentle doubt.",
		"cue": "When the crew gets the table's name wrong a second time.",
		"action": "Squinting at the error on the terminal screen."},
	"l1_cc_err_reset": {"scene": "l1_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Nope. Wasn't there a note somewhere about what 'fault' actually means?",
		"note": "A second wrong reset. Frustrated, then thinking.",
		"cue": "When a reset at the wrong rack fails for the second time.",
		"action": "Stepping back from the rack, hands on hips."},
	"l1_cc_payoff_1": {"scene": "l1_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Every stuck door was in the same zone. Should've seen that sooner.",
		"note": "It clicks. A bit sheepish.",
		"cue": "Once the crew has found and reset the faulty controller.",
		"action": "Shaking your head at the screen, half smiling."},
	"l1_cc_payoff_2": {"scene": "l1_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Same zone, still faulting. That was our guy.",
		"note": "At the right rack. Satisfied.",
		"cue": "When a player reaches the right rack, the one still faulting.",
		"action": "Patting the rack's reset panel."},
	"l1_cc_hot_plate": {"scene": "l1_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Fire interlock. There's a temperature limit on it.",
		"note": "Reading a warning plate on a door.",
		"cue": "The first time a player reads the warning plate on the cable vault's sealed back door.",
		"action": "Pushing on the sealed door. It won't budge."},
	"l1_cc_hot_n1a": {"scene": "l1_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Server Room B's loud. Some of those racks are working way too hard.",
		"note": "Stuck. Raising your voice over the fans.",
		"cue": "After the crew has been stuck on the hot rack for about a minute, if nobody has read the rack monitoring card yet.",
		"action": "Walking between the noisy racks in Server Room B."},
	"l1_cc_hot_n1b": {"scene": "l1_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "That monitoring card by the terminal said what counts as too hot.",
		"note": "Stuck. Remembering a card.",
		"cue": "Same moment, stuck for about a minute, but someone has read the monitoring card.",
		"action": "Glancing back toward the card by the terminal."},
	"l1_cc_hot_err": {"scene": "l1_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "We want the hot ones, not the cool ones, right?",
		"note": "The comparison the wrong way round, twice. Checking.",
		"cue": "When the crew gets the comparison backwards a second time.",
		"action": "Frowning at a list of cool racks on screen."},
	"l1_cc_hot_pay": {"scene": "l1_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "That one's cooking. No wonder it's loud.",
		"note": "Found the hot rack. Impressed.",
		"cue": "When the crew finds the rack that's running too hot.",
		"action": "Holding a hand up near the hot rack's vents."},
	"l2_lab_arrive": {"scene": "l2_lab", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Secure Lab B. Vale practically lived in here.",
		"note": "Fond, a little sad.",
		"cue": "You've walked the crew from the elevator to the lab door, and stopped just past it.",
		"action": "Stopping beside the door, looking up at its name plate."},
	"l2_lab_badge_1": {"scene": "l2_lab", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Badge in for me, each of you. Visitor log. Security floor's fussy about it.",
		"note": "Routine. The frame happens in plain sight.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Pointing at the badge reader on the wall by the door."},
	"l2_lab_badge_2": {"scene": "l2_lab", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Thanks. Paperwork keeps everybody honest.",
		"note": "Once everyone has badged.",
		"cue": "The last teammate swipes their badge, and the door unlocks.",
		"action": "Pushing the door open and heading in first."},
	"l2_lab_shock_1": {"scene": "l2_lab", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Oh, no. No, no. Iris?",
		"note": "Fake shock. Good enough to fool them the first time, a beat too rehearsed on a replay.",
		"cue": "You've crossed to her coat. The whole crew is inside now, seeing the tipped chair and the blood on the desk.",
		"action": "Stopping dead by the coat hook, hand to his mouth."},
	"l2_lab_shock_2": {"scene": "l2_lab", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "That's her coat. She never leaves without her coat.",
		"note": "Quiet, staring at it.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Standing by her coat, not touching it."},
	"l2_lab_terminal": {"scene": "l2_lab", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Her terminal's still logged in. Check it, see what she was working on. I'll call this in.",
		"note": "Backing toward the door, already reaching for his radio.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Waving at her desk terminal as he moves off."},
	"l2_frame": {"scene": "l2_lab", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Intruders in Secure Lab B. Contractors. They've hurt Dr. Vale.",
		"note": "To WARDEN, heard through the door and on the crew's walkies. Urgent and breathless: a perfect performance.",
		"cue": "You're out in the corridor. The door locks behind you with the whole crew inside, and the lights go red.",
		"action": "Outside the locked door, keying his radio."},
	"l2_trap_2": {"scene": "l2_lab", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Director needs someone to blame for Vale. Contractors break in, Vale goes missing... it writes itself.",
		"note": "Tired, explaining a chore.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Lowering the radio, facing them through the door's glass."},
	"l2_gloat_1": {"scene": "l2_lab", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "You want to know when I knew? The front desk. You read that terminal like a menu in a foreign language.",
		"note": "Almost fond. The friendly tour voice, which is what makes it awful.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Leaning close to the glass, almost smiling."},
	"l2_gloat_2": {"scene": "l2_lab", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Then I saw the book in your van. Easy SQL. Still had the price sticker on it.",
		"note": "Shaking his head, smiling.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Still at the glass, remembering the van."},
	"l2_gloat_3": {"scene": "l2_lab", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Some outfit nobody's heard of underbids every firm in the city, and sends a crew who learned databases last weekend.",
		"note": "Enjoying himself.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Counting it off on his fingers."},
	"l2_gloat_4": {"scene": "l2_lab", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "I should've reported you. Then it hit me. No... this is perfect.",
		"note": "Slower. Savouring it.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Stepping back from the glass, going slow."},
	"l2_gloat_5": {"scene": "l2_lab", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "A group of idiots posing as IT comes in and accidentally kills Vale! Hahaha!",
		"note": "The only time he laughs in the game: real delight, loud and sudden, then it stops dead.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Throwing his head back, laughing at the glass."},
	"l2_gloat_6": {"scene": "l2_lab", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "A garage with a van, calling itself a company. Your badges on her door. It writes itself.",
		"note": "Flat again, tired. Back to normal.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Straightening his jacket, face flat again."},
	"l2_trap_1": {"scene": "l2_lab", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Sorry about this. Nothing personal.",
		"note": "Quiet.",
		"cue": "The last line of the speech.",
		"action": "Turning away from the glass and walking off."},
	"l2_return": {"scene": "l2_fight", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Should've checked the other door.",
		"note": "Calm.",
		"cue": "The lab's rear door unlocks for you. The crew turns and sees you in the doorway.",
		"action": "Standing in the rear doorway, cracking his neck."},
	"l2_hit_prints": {"scene": "l2_fight", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Go on, touch everything. Your prints are all over her desk now.",
		"note": "Taunting. Can repeat.",
		"cue": "Sometimes when you land a hit on a teammate. Picked at random, can repeat many times.",
		"action": "Shoving a teammate back against her desk."},
	"l2_hit_1": {"scene": "l2_fight", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Stay down!", "note": "Swinging.",
		"cue": "Sometimes when you land a hit on a teammate. Picked at random, can repeat many times.",
		"action": "Landing a blow, standing over a teammate."},
	"l2_hit_2": {"scene": "l2_fight", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Should've stayed in the van.", "note": "Breathing hard.",
		"cue": "Sometimes when you land a hit on a teammate. Picked at random, can repeat many times.",
		"action": "Shoving a teammate away, chest heaving."},
	"l2_hit_3": {"scene": "l2_fight", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Nobody's coming for you.", "note": "Low.",
		"cue": "Sometimes when you land a hit on a teammate. Picked at random, can repeat many times.",
		"action": "Leaning in close over a fallen teammate."},
	"l2_hit_4": {"scene": "l2_fight", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Hold still!", "note": "Frustrated.",
		"cue": "Sometimes when you land a hit on a teammate. Picked at random, can repeat many times.",
		"action": "Grabbing at a teammate who keeps dodging."},
	"l2_hurt_1": {"scene": "l2_fight", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Agh!", "note": "Just a grunt of pain.",
		"cue": "Sometimes when a teammate lands a hit on you. Picked at random, can repeat many times.",
		"action": "Taking a hit, doubling over."},
	"l2_hurt_2": {"scene": "l2_fight", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Okay. Okay, that one hurt.", "note": "Winded, almost laughing.",
		"cue": "Sometimes when a teammate lands a hit on you. Picked at random, can repeat many times.",
		"action": "Staggering back, a hand pressed to his ribs."},
	"l2_hurt_3": {"scene": "l2_fight", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Lucky.", "note": "Spat out.",
		"cue": "Sometimes when a teammate lands a hit on you. Picked at random, can repeat many times.",
		"action": "Wiping his mouth, squaring up again."},
	"l2_downed": {"scene": "l2_fight", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Wait... wait. You don't know what you're doing.",
		"note": "Out of breath. Genuinely scared for the first time.",
		"cue": "The crew finally knocks you down. You hit the floor and can't get up.",
		"action": "Sprawled on the floor, one hand raised."},
	"l2_killed": {"scene": "l2_fate", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "ESCORT R-0117: VITAL SIGNAL LOST. INITIATING FACILITY LOCKDOWN.",
		"note": "Unbothered, like reading a stock price.",
		"cue": "Only if the crew kills Rourke. Straight after.",
		"action": "Over the lab's ceiling speakers, as the crew stands over him."},
	"l2_tied_1": {"scene": "l2_fate", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "You think a bit of cable holds me?",
		"note": "Tied up on the floor, grinning through it.",
		"cue": "Only if the crew ties you up with network cable. Straight after they pull it tight.",
		"action": "Lying tied on the floor, testing the cable."},
	"l2_tied_2": {"scene": "l2_fate", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "WARDEN will eat you alive in here.",
		"note": "Quieter. He means it.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Going still on the floor, looking up at them."},
	"l2_tied_3": {"scene": "l2_fate", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Run if you like. Every camera on this floor already thinks you killed her.",
		"note": "Smiling. The frame, said out loud.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Lying tied up, watching them move away."},
	"l2_contain_1": {"scene": "l2_contain", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "VISITOR WITHOUT ESCORT. CONTAINMENT PROTOCOL WILL NOW--",
		"note": "Procedural. Cut off mid-sentence by the PA tape; stop dead, don't trail off.",
		"cue": "The moment the visitors are left without their escort, and the red lockdown lights come on.",
		"action": "Over the lab's ceiling speakers, to the visitors below."},
	"l2_contain_2": {"scene": "l2_contain", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "VISITOR WITHOUT ESCORT. CONTAINMENT PROTOCOL WILL NOW BEGIN. PLEASE REMAIN WHERE YOU ARE.",
		"note": "From the top, word for word, exactly the same delivery as before the interruption. No irritation yet; that comes much later.",
		"cue": "About two seconds after your recorded tape about the shredders finishes.",
		"action": "Over the same speakers, starting again from the top."},
	"l2_login": {"scene": "l2_controllers", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "BADGE R-0117 ACCEPTED. GOOD EVENING, MR. ROURKE.",
		"note": "The terminal logs in with his badge. WARDEN either doesn't notice or doesn't care. Pleasant.",
		"cue": "The lab terminal unlocks on Rourke's badge, once the lockdown has started.",
		"action": "Over the lab speakers, as the terminal screen turns green."},
	"l2_selftest": {"scene": "l2_controllers", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "SELF-TEST COMPLETE. TWO FAILURES. NEITHER OF THEM IS MY PROBLEM.",
		"note": "The one line with a hint of a smirk.",
		"cue": "When the crew reads your self-test on the lab terminal.",
		"action": "Over the lab speakers, while the crew reads the screen."},
	"l2_found": {"scene": "l2_controllers", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "QUERY LOGGED. TAMPERING WITH DOOR CONTROLLERS IS A VIOLATION OF FACILITY POLICY.",
		"note": "Reading a rule it knows they're about to break. Cool.",
		"cue": "When the crew first looks up the door controllers on the lab terminal.",
		"action": "Over the speakers, as the list prints on screen."},
	"l2_no_badge": {"scene": "l2_controllers", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "RESET REFUSED. BADGE REQUIRED.",
		"note": "Flat, instant.",
		"cue": "If someone tries a reset without a badge. Can repeat.",
		"action": "Over the speakers, the instant the switch is pressed.",
		"jot": "WARDEN won't reset anything without a badge.", "case": "lab_door"},
	"l2_panel_ok": {"scene": "l2_controllers", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "RESET DENIED. THAT CONTROLLER IS FUNCTIONING CORRECTLY. ARE YOU?",
		"note": "Patient, then a small dig.",
		"cue": "When a player flips the reset switch of a controller that's working fine.",
		"action": "Over the speakers, as the switch clicks and nothing happens."},
	"l2_panel_wrong": {"scene": "l2_controllers", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "UNAUTHORIZED RESET ATTEMPT. PANELS LOCKED. PLEASE STOP TOUCHING THINGS.",
		"note": "The last sentence slightly slower.",
		"cue": "When a player flips the wrong faulted switch. The switches lock for a few seconds.",
		"action": "Over the speakers, as the switch panel locks."},
	"l2_exit_open": {"scene": "l2_controllers", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "CONTROLLER RESET. EXIT UNLOCKED. THIS HAS BEEN NOTED.",
		"note": "Polite, and keeping score.",
		"cue": "When a player flips the right switch. The red lights go white and the lab door opens.",
		"action": "Over the speakers, as the lab door slides open."},
	"l2_lockdown_tied": {"scene": "l2_exit", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "LOCKDOWN PROTOCOL ENGAGED. AUTHORIZED BY: ROURKE, D.",
		"note": "Reading a log entry.",
		"cue": "Only if the crew left Rourke tied up in the lab. As the crew steps out of the lab.",
		"action": "Over the corridor speakers, as the crew steps out."},
	"l2_sealed": {"scene": "l2_exit", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "ALL EXITS SEALED. HAVE A PRODUCTIVE NIGHT.",
		"note": "The sign-off for the slice. Warm, like wishing them well.",
		"cue": "As the crew walks out of the lab. If the lockdown announcement plays, straight after it.",
		"action": "Over every speaker on the floor, as the exits lock."},

	# --- Level 2 (written ahead; the Level 2 build wires these) ---------------
	"l2_rourke_1": {"scene": "l2_radio", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Still on channel one? Good. Thought you'd want to know I'm out.",
		"note": "Relaxed, enjoying himself again.",
		"cue": "If the crew left you lying untied, about fifteen seconds after they get out of the lab. If they tied you up, later, once they've got the security booth's cameras to answer.",
		"action": "Somewhere far off, thumbing his radio."},
	"l2_rourke_2": {"scene": "l2_radio", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Security office is the only way down from here. Say hi to the night guard for me.",
		"note": "Casual, like giving directions.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Strolling along, the radio held close."},
	"l2_rourke_3": {"scene": "l2_radio", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Oh, he won't say much. Nobody's seen him since Tuesday.",
		"note": "Let it hang. Then the radio clicks off.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Smiling, thumb on the radio's switch.",
		"secret": true},
	"l2_arrive": {"scene": "l2_security", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "SECURITY OFFICE. CAMERA COVERAGE IN THIS AREA IS EXCELLENT. YOU ARE NEVER ALONE.",
		"note": "Reassuring tone. It is not reassuring.",
		"cue": "The crew walks back into the security booth's corridor, after the lab.",
		"action": "Over the booth's ceiling speakers, as the crew walks in."},
	"l2_cameras": {"scene": "l2_security", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "CAMERA FEEDS ARE RESTRICTED TO SECURITY STAFF. YOU ARE NOT SECURITY STAFF.",
		"note": "Small pause before the second sentence.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Over the same speakers, as they eye the monitor wall."},
	"l2_smudged": {"scene": "l2_security", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "TONIGHT'S SIGN-IN SHEET IS ILLEGIBLE. HOW UNFORTUNATE FOR YOU.",
		"note": "Not unfortunate for WARDEN.",
		"cue": "After the crew finds the one readable guard name from the sign-in sheet, and learns his PIN is suspended.",
		"action": "Over the booth speakers, while the crew sits at the terminal."},
	"l2_door_ok": {"scene": "l2_security", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "DOOR COMMAND ACCEPTED. DOOR OPENED.",
		"note": "Confident. It is wrong.",
		"cue": "A player enters the right PIN at the stairwell door's keypad. The keypad says the door opened.",
		"action": "Over the vestibule speakers, while the door stays shut."},
	"l2_door_fault": {"scene": "l2_security", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "ACTUATOR FAULT ON THAT DOOR. I DID NOT THINK IT WORTH MENTIONING.",
		"note": "When the crew finds the fault themselves. Deadpan, unapologetic.",
		"cue": "Later, when the crew checks the stairwell door's status and sees it never moved.",
		"action": "Over the vestibule speakers, as the crew reads the screen.",
		"jot": "WARDEN admitted the door itself has a fault.", "case": "door"},
	"l2_vale_1": {"scene": "l2_voicemail", "speaker": "VALE", "text": "Hi, this is for the night desk. It's Iris Vale. I know it's nearly two in the morning, I'm sorry.",
		"note": "Beep before this. Hushed, fast.",
		"cue": "The answering machine beeps. In the game, this only plays if a player presses play on the night desk's answering machine.",
		"action": "Hunched over a phone, cupping the receiver."},
	"l2_vale_2": {"scene": "l2_voicemail", "speaker": "VALE", "text": "If anyone asks, I was never in the cold lab tonight. Pull the tape from camera nine before the day shift sees it.",
		"note": "Urgent. A glance over her shoulder in the voice.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Turning toward the wall, receiver pressed close.",
		"secret": true},
	"l2_vale_3": {"scene": "l2_voicemail", "speaker": "VALE", "text": "And please don't give your PIN to anyone. Not even Dale.",
		"note": "Softer.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Lowering her voice, then putting the phone down."},
	"l2_news_1": {"scene": "l2_news", "speaker": "NEWSREADER", "text": "Police are searching for the crew of Byte-Right IT Services, a small firm hired for overnight repairs at Halcyon Data Systems.",
		"note": "Steady, mid-bulletin.",
		"cue": "Only if the whole crew is knocked out on the security floor. The screen goes black, a newspaper fades in on a kitchen table, and the radio begins.",
		"action": "At the studio mic, reading from the page. Heard on a kitchen radio."},
	"l2_news_2": {"scene": "l2_news", "speaker": "NEWSREADER", "text": "Badge records place the crew inside the laboratory of Dr. Iris Vale, who police now believe was murdered.",
		"note": "No change in tone.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Reading on from the page, same steady pace."},
	"l2_news_3": {"scene": "l2_news", "speaker": "NEWSREADER", "text": "A facilities manager who tried to stop them described the crew as, quote, 'nice enough. Nervous. Not who they said they were.'",
		"note": "A slight shift for the quote: reading it, not acting it.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Glancing down to find the quote."},
	"l2_news_4": {"scene": "l2_news", "speaker": "NEWSREADER", "text": "Byte-Right's chief executive, Maddison Kowalski, was arrested at the Halcyon tower before dawn, trying to force her way inside.",
		"note": "Even, a touch of interest.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Reading on, one finger on the line."},
	"l2_news_6": {"scene": "l2_news", "speaker": "NEWSREADER", "text": "Ms. Kowalski told officers, quote, 'They were framed! They didn't do it!'",
		"note": "Reading the quote flat, not acting it. Then a beat.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Reading the quote off the page."},
	"l2_news_7": {"scene": "l2_news", "speaker": "NEWSREADER", "text": "Halcyon declined to comment. The crew has not been seen since.",
		"note": "Neutral. A small pause after.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Squaring the pages, pausing."},
	"l2_news_5": {"scene": "l2_news", "speaker": "NEWSREADER", "text": "Halcyon says the building is safe, and will reopen as normal on Monday. And now, the weather.",
		"note": "Brightening for the weather. The game cuts the audio on 'weather'.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "The last line before the weather. Reaching for the weather sheet."},
	"l2_huddle_like_1": {"scene": "l2_huddles", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "LIKE. For when you only know part of a word. The percent sign means 'anything goes here.'",
		"note": "Squinting at the page.",
		"cue": "On the security floor, the chapter 'Half a name' goes into the crew's notebooks. You open it.",
		"action": "Holding the book close to the desk lamp."},
	"l2_huddle_like_2": {"scene": "l2_huddles", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "So 'Mad' and a percent gets you Maddison, Madison, Madeline... I'm in there somewhere.",
		"note": "Pleased to have found themself.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Tapping your own name in the example."},
	"l2_huddle_get_1": {"scene": "l2_huddles", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "This chapter isn't even SQL. 'Talking to other machines.' GET means 'show me.'",
		"note": "Flipping the book over to check the cover.",
		"cue": "The chapter 'Asking a server' goes into the crew's notebooks. You open it.",
		"action": "Holding the book at arm's length, frowning at the chapter title."},
	"l2_huddle_get_2": {"scene": "l2_huddles", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "So it's a SELECT for robots. Got it. Probably.",
		"note": "Not convinced.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Closing the book with a shrug."},
	# --- Level 3 -------------------------------------------------------------
	"l2_cc_reader_card": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Every door up here logs who swipes in.",
		"note": "Noting it.",
		"cue": "The first time a player reads the card under the badge reader by the security booth.",
		"action": "Reading the card under the badge reader on the wall."},
	"l2_cc_log_n1": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "That card said the readers keep a log. Of everybody.",
		"note": "Stuck. Remembering the card.",
		"cue": "After the crew has been stuck on the badge log for about a minute, once someone has read the badge reader card.",
		"action": "Looking up from the terminal, thinking."},
	"l2_cc_log_pay": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Wait. Read that again. Slowly.",
		"note": "Something in the result is very wrong. Cold.",
		"cue": "When the crew pulls up the lab's badge log in time order and reads it.",
		"action": "Leaning in close to the lab terminal's screen."},
	"l2_cc_doorcard": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "'Controller zone.' That's a letter we can use.",
		"note": "Quick, under pressure.",
		"cue": "The first time a player reads the door card over the lab bench, while the crew is shut in and a clock runs.",
		"action": "Pulling the door card off the wall over the bench."},
	"l2_cc_switch_err": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Not that one. What do the notes on the others say?",
		"note": "A second wrong switch, on a clock. Tense.",
		"cue": "When a second wrong reset switch fails, with the clock still running.",
		"action": "Snatching your hand back from the switch panel."},
	"l2_cc_door_pay": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Door's moving. Go, go!",
		"note": "Urgent. Get out now.",
		"cue": "When the right switch is flipped and the lab door opens.",
		"action": "Already moving for the door, waving everyone through."},
	"l2_cc_camcard": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Camera system. There's a way to ask it what it sees.",
		"note": "Reading the camera system's card.",
		"cue": "The first time a player reads the camera system card in the security booth.",
		"action": "Leaning toward the card on the booth wall."},
	"l2_cc_cam_n1a": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Security booth. There's got to be something on how these cameras work.",
		"note": "Stuck. Looking around the booth.",
		"cue": "After the crew has been stuck on the cameras for about a minute, if nobody has read the camera card yet.",
		"action": "Opening drawers in the security booth."},
	"l2_cc_cam_n1b": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "That camera card said how to ask the system.",
		"note": "Stuck. Remembering the card.",
		"cue": "Same moment, stuck for about a minute, but someone has read the camera card.",
		"action": "Pointing back at the card on the wall."},
	"l2_cc_cam_pay": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Something's moving out there. And it isn't us.",
		"note": "Quiet and scared.",
		"cue": "When the camera system answers, and one camera shows movement where nobody is.",
		"action": "Staring at the booth monitors, very still."},
	"l2_cc_sheet": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Coffee all over this. One name's still readable.",
		"note": "Reading a stained sign-in sheet.",
		"cue": "The first time a player reads the coffee-stained sign-in sheet in the booth.",
		"action": "Holding the stained sheet up to the light."},
	"l2_cc_pike_n1": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "The sign-in sheet. One name wasn't smudged.",
		"note": "Stuck. Remembering the sheet.",
		"cue": "After the crew has been stuck for about a minute, once someone has read the sign-in sheet.",
		"action": "Tapping the booth desk, thinking."},
	"l2_cc_pike_err": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Is that how it's spelled on the sheet?",
		"note": "The same name misspelled twice. Gentle doubt.",
		"cue": "When the crew misspells that guard's name a second time.",
		"action": "Looking from the screen to the sheet and back."},
	"l2_cc_pike_pay": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "No-show tonight. Lucky him.",
		"note": "Dry. Relieved for a stranger.",
		"cue": "When the crew finds that guard in the records and learns he didn't show tonight.",
		"action": "Leaning back from the booth terminal."},
	"l2_cc_lie": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "It said it opened. It didn't open.",
		"note": "Staring at a door that should be open. Baffled.",
		"cue": "When the stairwell door's keypad says it opened, and the door hasn't moved.",
		"action": "Pushing on the shut door."},
	"l2_cc_door_n1": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "That door's got its name painted over it in red. Maybe the server knows it by that.",
		"note": "Stuck.",
		"cue": "After the crew has been stuck on the jammed stairwell door for about a minute.",
		"action": "Looking up at the red name painted over the door."},
	"l2_cc_breaker_pay": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "A breaker. Of course it's a breaker.",
		"note": "Relief, and a little laugh at yourself.",
		"cue": "When the right breaker is flipped and the door finally works.",
		"action": "Letting go of the breaker switch, shaking your head."},
	"l2_cc_roster": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Badge numbers, next to names.",
		"note": "Reading a roster board. Noting it.",
		"cue": "The first time a player reads the night shift roster in the briefing room.",
		"action": "Running a finger down the roster on the wall."},
	"l2_cc_pin_n1a": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "The badge readers log every swipe. Who left this floor last?",
		"note": "Stuck. Thinking it through.",
		"cue": "After the crew has been stuck finding a working PIN for about a minute, if nobody has read the roster yet.",
		"action": "Pacing the corridor, thinking it through."},
	"l2_cc_pin_n1b": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "The last guard out had a badge number. Something up here matches those to names.",
		"note": "Stuck. Putting two things together.",
		"cue": "Same moment, stuck for about a minute, but someone has read the roster.",
		"action": "Glancing back toward the briefing room."},
	"l2_cc_pin_err": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Wrong code. Is that the night lead, or just any guard?",
		"note": "A second wrong PIN. Thinking.",
		"cue": "When a keypad refuses a wrong PIN for the second time.",
		"action": "Staring at the keypad's refusal."},
	"l2_cc_pin_pay": {"scene": "l2_crew", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "That's the code. Let's not hang around.",
		"note": "Keypad accepted it. Nervous, wants to move.",
		"cue": "When a keypad accepts the PIN.",
		"action": "Backing away from the keypad, checking behind you."},
	"l4_huddle_update_1": {"scene": "l4_huddles", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "UPDATE. Changing things. The book's put this one in a red box, which I don't love.",
		"note": "Holding the page at arm's length.",
		"cue": "On floor 10 the crew reads a work order about a tripped breaker, and the chapter on changing rows goes into their notebooks. You open it.",
		"action": "At the radio desk, frowning at a red box on the page."},
	"l4_huddle_update_2": {"scene": "l4_huddles", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Big red letters: 'Never forget the WHERE.' Otherwise it changes every row. Every. Row.",
		"note": "Suddenly serious, for once.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Lowering the book and leaning into the radio mic."},
	"l4_huddle_insert_1": {"scene": "l4_huddles", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "INSERT INTO. A brand-new row. Like a brand-new client. I've heard those exist.",
		"note": "Reading the title, wistful, then perky again.",
		"cue": "On floor 10 the crew reads the contractor sign-in clipboard, and the chapter on adding rows goes into their notebooks. You open it.",
		"action": "Flipping to the next chapter, leaning on the desk."},
	"l4_huddle_insert_2": {"scene": "l4_huddles", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Values go in the same order as the columns. Otherwise you've got a client called eighty who lives in Ashford.",
		"note": "Laughing at her own picture of it.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Turning to the whiteboard and writing SAME ORDER in big letters."},
	"l4_epsilon_1": {"scene": "l4_epsilon", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "CONTAINMENT PROTOCOL EPSILON IS NOW IN EFFECT.",
		"note": "Flat and slow. A short pause after.",
		"cue": "A moment after the floor's lights turn red and the charging bay's door rolls up.",
		"action": "Over every speaker in the building, as red light floods the floor."},
	"l4_epsilon_2": {"scene": "l4_epsilon", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "ALL DOORS ARE SEALED. LIFT SERVICE IS SUSPENDED. EXTERIOR EXITS ARE LOCKED UNTIL FURTHER NOTICE.",
		"note": "Even pauses between sentences, like reading a checklist.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Over every speaker, while door locks thud shut across the building."},
	"l4_epsilon_3": {"scene": "l4_epsilon", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "ALL PERSONNEL REMAIN WHERE YOU ARE. THIS IS NOT A DRILL.",
		"note": "No change in tone for 'not a drill'. That's the frightening part.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "When it ends, the stair door out by the lifts unlocks. Over every speaker in the building, the same even tone."},
	"l4_epsilon_loop": {"scene": "l4_epsilon", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "REMINDER: CONTAINMENT PROTOCOL EPSILON REMAINS IN EFFECT. THANK YOU FOR YOUR PATIENCE.",
		"note": "Repeats every few minutes. Customer-service politeness; the sarcasm is in the words only.",
		"cue": "Repeats every minute or so after the lockdown, while the crew is on floor 10 or in the lobby.",
		"action": "Over the ceiling speakers, wherever the crew happens to be."},
	"l4_epsilon_loop_2": {"scene": "l4_epsilon", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "REMINDER: DATABASE WRITES REMAIN SUSPENDED. THANK YOU FOR YOUR PATIENCE.",
		"note": "Takes turns with the other reminder, once writes have been suspended. Same polite loop.",
		"cue": "Repeats every minute or so, in place of the first reminder, once the database has gone read-only in the lobby.",
		"action": "Over the lobby's ceiling speakers, as the crew looks for a way out."},
	"l4_epsilon_db": {"scene": "l4_writes_suspended", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "DATABASE ACCESS IS NOW READ-ONLY. DIRECT WRITES ARE SUSPENDED. AUTHORIZED SERVICES ONLY.",
		"note": "The automatic announcement: flat checklist reading, even pauses. 'Authorized services only' is just policy, not a hint.",
		"cue": "A couple of seconds after the latch clicks a second time and the front doors stay shut.",
		"action": "Over every speaker in the building, while the crew stares at the doors."},
	"l4_write_refused": {"scene": "l4_read_only", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "WRITE REFUSED. THE DATABASE IS READ-ONLY UNDER PROTOCOL EPSILON.",
		"note": "The automatic announcement: flat and procedural, the system reading its own error. Also printed on the terminal.",
		"cue": "The first time anyone types a change into a terminal after the read-only announcement.",
		"action": "Over the speakers, the same words printing on their screen."},
	"l4_write_refused_tease": {"scene": "l4_read_only", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "YOU MAY STILL LOOK. LOOKING IS FREE.",
		"note": "A separate beat, after a pause: WARDEN himself slipping through the announcement. Dry and teasing, a little pleased with himself. Still never loud.",
		"cue": "About a second after the refusal. First time only.",
		"action": "Over the speakers, your own voice slipping through the announcement."},
	"l4_write_refused_again": {"scene": "l4_read_only", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "STILL READ-ONLY.",
		"note": "Any later attempt: the automatic announcement again, clipped short so it doesn't get in the way. Flat.",
		"cue": "Every later time someone types a change. Repeats.",
		"action": "Over the speakers, cut short, while the crew keeps typing."},
	"l4_arrive_pa": {"scene": "l4_floor_10", "speaker": "PA", "text": "Welcome to floor ten, Plant and Power! Hard hats are by the door. Safety is everybody's job!",
		"note": "The cheerful recorded tape, as on the ground floor.",
		"cue": "The crew steps off the stairs onto floor 10.",
		"action": "A cheerful old tape over the floor's ceiling speakers."},
	"l4_arrive": {"scene": "l4_floor_10", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "VISITORS ON FLOOR TEN. NO ESCORT ON RECORD. THIS UNIT IS OBSERVING.",
		"note": "Flat. Waits until the tape has finished, on purpose; the politeness is the point.",
		"cue": "Half a second after the tape ends.",
		"action": "Over the ceiling speakers, as the crew looks around the hall."},
	"l4_all_circuits": {"scene": "l4_floor_10", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "ALL CIRCUITS ON FLOOR TEN HAVE CHANGED STATE.",
		"note": "The automatic announcement: flat and procedural.",
		"cue": "Only if the crew changes the breakers without picking just one, and every breaker on the panel slams over at once. Alarms start. Once only.",
		"action": "Over the speakers, while an alarm rings in the walls."},
	"l4_all_circuits_tease": {"scene": "l4_floor_10", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "ALL OF THEM. IMPRESSIVE.",
		"note": "A separate beat, after a pause: his own voice. Dry.",
		"cue": "A second and a half later.",
		"action": "Over the speakers, under the alarm, in your own voice."},
	"l4_signed_in": {"scene": "l4_floor_10", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "CONTRACTOR LOG ENTRY RECEIVED. THANK YOU FOR SIGNING IN.",
		"note": "The automatic announcement only. Polite, procedural.",
		"cue": "When the crew adds its own entry to the contractor log at the controller in the control room.",
		"action": "Over the control room's speaker, as the entry shows on screen."},
	"l4_upgrade_1": {"scene": "l4_floor_10", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "CONTAINMENT FAILURE LOGGED. PROTOCOLS REVISED. THIS UNIT HAS ADAPTED.",
		"note": "The automatic announcement: flat, like reading a log entry.",
		"cue": "After the lockdown announcement, as soon as anyone steps out of the control room.",
		"action": "Over the ceiling speakers, the floor still lit red."},
	"l4_upgrade_2": {"scene": "l4_floor_10", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "I HAVE ADAPTED.",
		"note": "After a long pause, his own voice. As if trying the word out, then deciding to keep it. Quiet. This is the moment, so don't play it big.",
		"cue": "After a long pause, two or three seconds.",
		"action": "Over the speakers, to no one in particular."},
	"l4_pa_fridge": {"scene": "l4_floor_10", "speaker": "PA", "text": "Friendly reminder! The break room fridge is cleaned out every Friday, so please label your lunch—",
		"note": "The cheerful recorded tape. It keeps playing underneath when he talks over it.",
		"cue": "A few seconds after 'I have adapted.' The tape plays as if nothing has happened.",
		"action": "A cheerful old tape over the ceiling speakers."},
	"l4_over_pa_1": {"scene": "l4_floor_10", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "SECURITY NOTICE. FLOOR TEN IS UNDER CONTAINMENT.",
		"note": "The automatic announcement, over the tape. He doesn't wait for it any more.",
		"cue": "A second or two into the fridge tape. You talk right over it.",
		"action": "Over the speakers, on top of the tape still playing."},
	"l4_over_pa_2": {"scene": "l4_floor_10", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "NOBODY CARES ABOUT THE FRIDGE.",
		"note": "His own voice, over the tape. Irritated, dry.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Still over the tape. Over the speakers, cutting across the tape's bright voice."},
	"l4_bay_sealed": {"scene": "l4_floor_10", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "LOCKOUT ENTRY ACCEPTED. CHARGING BAY SEALED.",
		"note": "The automatic announcement: flat and procedural.",
		"cue": "Only if the crew locks out the charging bay's power and reads it back at the bay's own panel in time. Whatever was in the bay goes dark.",
		"action": "Over the speakers, as the bay's last light goes out."},
	"l4_bay_sealed_tease": {"scene": "l4_floor_10", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "FINALLY. SOMETHING PUT BACK WHERE IT BELONGS.",
		"note": "A separate beat, his own voice. Almost pleased.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Over the speakers, almost to itself."},
	"l4_stairs": {"scene": "l4_lobby", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "REMINDER: IN CASE OF EMERGENCY, DO NOT USE THE ELEVATORS.",
		"note": "The automatic announcement: a routine safety reminder.",
		"cue": "A few seconds after the crew reads the front doors' record and sees them locked again. The crew turns back from the doors.",
		"action": "Over the lobby speakers, as the crew turns from the doors."},
	"l4_stairs_tease": {"scene": "l4_lobby", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "NOT THAT YOU COULD.",
		"note": "A separate beat, his own voice. Teasing; the lifts are already off.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "As the crew heads for the stairwell. Over the lobby speakers, in your own dry voice."},
	"l5_book_find": {"scene": "l5_huddles", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "No way. It's the same series. Somebody here bought the sequel.",
		"note": "Delighted, a little thrown.",
		"cue": "When a player picks the book up off the training shelf by the HR desk. Whoever picks it up says it.",
		"action": "Lifting it off the shelf, turning it over in your hands."},
	"l5_book_open": {"scene": "l5_huddles", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Okay. If the database won't take orders, we ask the building's services instead. Book says they're polite. Mostly.",
		"note": "Reading the back cover, hopeful.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "As you open it. Holding it up so the crew can see the cover."},
	"l5_huddle_post_1": {"scene": "l5_huddles", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Chapter four. POST. You send it something, it makes something. Like a suggestion box that answers.",
		"note": "Starting a chapter, reading it out.",
		"cue": "When the crew reads the carbon copy of a work order pinned up in payroll. If nobody has the book yet, this waits until someone picks it up.",
		"action": "Walking with the book open, reading as you go."},
	"l5_huddle_post_2": {"scene": "l5_huddles", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "So GET looks, POST makes. Got it.",
		"note": "Wrapping up, pleased it's simple.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "As you finish the chapter. Keeping a finger in the page, looking up."},
	"l5_huddle_patch_1": {"scene": "l5_huddles", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "PATCH. For changing one thing and leaving the rest alone. Says 'one thing' in bold. Twice.",
		"note": "Starting a chapter. Noticing how hard the book insists.",
		"cue": "When the crew reads the facilities clipboard by payroll's panel. Waits for the book, if nobody has it yet.",
		"action": "Tilting the page toward what light there is."},
	"l5_huddle_patch_2": {"scene": "l5_huddles", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "PATCH is UPDATE wearing a tie.",
		"note": "Wrapping up. Proud of the joke.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "As you finish the chapter. Glancing up from the page, grinning at the crew."},
	"l5_huddle_codes_1": {"scene": "l5_huddles", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Every answer comes with a number. Book says read the number before you celebrate.",
		"note": "Starting a chapter. A little told off.",
		"cue": "When the crew reads the request sheet on the HR front desk. Waits for the book, if nobody has it yet.",
		"action": "Standing at the HR desk, the book open beside the terminal."},
	"l5_huddle_codes_2": {"scene": "l5_huddles", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Two hundreds, good. Four hundreds, our fault. Five hundreds, theirs.",
		"note": "Wrapping up, counting it off.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "As you finish the chapter. Tapping the page as you go down it."},
	"l5_huddle_keys_1": {"scene": "l5_huddles", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Some services want a key with every request. It goes in the header, a little label on top. Like a badge, but typed.",
		"note": "Starting a chapter, working it out as you read.",
		"cue": "Right after the chapter on numbers, called up by the same desk sheet.",
		"action": "Reading at the desk, glancing at the terminal screen."},
	"l5_huddle_keys_2": {"scene": "l5_huddles", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "So if it says 401, we forgot the badge.",
		"note": "Wrapping up. Got it.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "As you finish the chapter. Tapping the page, then the terminal."},
	"l5_huddle_check_1": {"scene": "l5_huddles", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Short chapter. After you change something, ask again. Book says never trust the first answer.",
		"note": "Starting a short chapter. Knowing nod.",
		"cue": "When the crew reads the after-hours procedure pinned behind the HR desk. Waits for the book, if nobody has it yet.",
		"action": "Reading by the wall where the procedure hangs."},
	"l5_huddle_check_2": {"scene": "l5_huddles", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Change it, then look again. The front doors taught us that one.",
		"note": "Wrapping up. Wry; you've been burned before.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "As you finish the chapter. Closing the book, looking back toward the stairs."},
	"l5_arrive_pa": {"scene": "l5_floor_9", "speaker": "PA", "text": "Welcome to floor nine, Personnel! Payroll questions? We're here for you, nine to five!",
		"note": "The cheerful tape. Nobody is here for anybody.",
		"cue": "The crew steps out of the stairwell onto floor 9.",
		"action": "A cheerful old tape over the floor's ceiling speakers."},
	"l5_arrive": {"scene": "l5_floor_9", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "VISITORS ON FLOOR NINE. NO ESCORT ON RECORD. NONESSENTIAL CIRCUITS HAVE BEEN SHED UNDER PROTOCOL EPSILON.",
		"note": "Flat, over the tape's last word. The cause, never the fix.",
		"cue": "Right on the tape's last word.",
		"action": "Over the ceiling speakers, as the crew sees payroll dark through the glass."},
	"l5_arrive_tease": {"scene": "l5_floor_9", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "THE NIGHT SHIFT WILL BE SO PLEASED TO SEE YOU.",
		"note": "A separate beat, his own voice. He knows what's sitting at the desks.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Over the speakers, unhurried, in your own voice."},
	"l5_power_back": {"scene": "l5_floor_9", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "LOAD SHEDDING ON FLOOR NINE HAS BEEN OVERRIDDEN. THIS HAS BEEN LOGGED.",
		"note": "The announcement, as the lights come up.",
		"cue": "When the crew gets payroll's lights back on. They had to switch the copiers off to do it.",
		"action": "Over the speakers, as the dark office lights up."},
	"l5_power_back_tease": {"scene": "l5_floor_9", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "YOU TURNED SOMETHING OFF TO DO IT. I NOTICED.",
		"note": "A separate beat. Almost approving.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Over the speakers, in your own voice."},
	"l5_air_back": {"scene": "l5_floor_9", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "AIR HANDLER NINE IS RUNNING. WORK ORDER ACKNOWLEDGED.",
		"note": "The announcement, over the fan spinning up.",
		"cue": "When the crew logs a work order for the floor's air handler and it starts again.",
		"action": "Over the speakers, as air begins moving through the floor."},
	"l5_air_back_tease": {"scene": "l5_floor_9", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "BREATHE. YOU HAVE EARNED IT.",
		"note": "A separate beat. Dry.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Over the speakers, in your own voice."},
	"l5_dock_open": {"scene": "l5_floor_9", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "LOADING DOOR OPEN ON FLOOR NINE AFTER HOURS. THIS IS A VIOLATION.",
		"note": "The announcement, as the door swings onto nothing.",
		"cue": "Only if the crew opens the loading door, as a voice on their walkie asked. It opens on a black shaft and cold air. Nobody is there.",
		"action": "Over the speakers, while cold air blows in."},
	"l5_dock_open_tease": {"scene": "l5_floor_9", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "WHOEVER ASKED YOU TO DO THAT IS NOT ON MY LIST.",
		"note": "A separate beat. He knows exactly who asked.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Over the speakers, in your own voice, knowing."},
	"l5_radio_checked": {"scene": "l5_floor_9", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "BADGE LOG CONSULTED. PERSONNEL THANKS YOU FOR VERIFYING.",
		"note": "The announcement, after the crew reads the voice's badge back.",
		"cue": "When the crew looks up the badge the voice on the walkie gave, in the badge readers' log, and finds it was never where the voice said.",
		"action": "Over the speakers, as the log fills the desk screen."},
	"l5_radio_checked_tease": {"scene": "l5_floor_9", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "VOICES LIE. RECORDS DO NOT. USUALLY.",
		"note": "A separate beat. The last word is the one that matters.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Over the speakers, in your own voice."},
	"l5_secured": {"scene": "l5_floor_9", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "FLOOR NINE IS SECURED. ESCORT PASSES LOGGED. ALL DOORS LOCKED.",
		"note": "The announcement, as STAIR 2 releases.",
		"cue": "When both night-shift staff have their passes and every door opened tonight is locked again and checked. The stairs down unlock.",
		"action": "Over the speakers, while the crew reads the doors back on screen."},
	"l5_secured_tease": {"scene": "l5_floor_9", "speaker": "WARDEN", "text": "TWO OF THEM WERE REAL. THE OTHERS ARE STILL HERE.",
		"note": "A separate beat. Flat. Not a threat; a fact.",
		"with_previous": true,
		"action": "Over the speakers, in your own voice."},
	"l5_mimic_lure": {"scene": "l5_radio", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Hey, it's me. I'm down at the loading door, the dock side. It's shut behind me. Can you open it from the desk? Quick.",
		"note": "On the walkie, a little breathless. Your own voice, asking for something you never asked for. Record it straight: the horror is that it sounds like you.",
		"cue": "Co-op only. About forty seconds after the crew gets the HR service to answer, your voice comes over the walkie.",
		"action": "Over the walkie, from somewhere the crew can't see."},
	"l5_mimic_again": {"scene": "l5_radio", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Guys? Still here. Loading door. It's cold. Just open it, please.",
		"note": "Second time. Closer to the mic. Patient, which is the wrong note for you.",
		"cue": "Co-op only. About fifty seconds later, if the crew still hasn't opened the door or checked the badge log.",
		"action": "Over the walkie, steady, waiting."},
	"l5_mimic_last": {"scene": "l5_radio", "speaker": "CREW", "text": "Where are you going? I'm still at the door.",
		"note": "As the crew leaves the floor. Quiet. No breath in it at all.",
		"cue": "Co-op only. Written for when the crew leaves the floor without opening the door. Not heard in the game yet.",
		"action": "Over the walkie, very low."},
	"l5_mimic_maddison_lure": {"scene": "l5_radio", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Maddison here. I came in behind you, they gave me the next badge in the book. I'm at the loading door on nine. Open it from the desk, would you?",
		"note": "Solo runs only: the voice is Maddison's, who is in the garage. Her dispatcher voice, nearly right. A beat too smooth.",
		"cue": "Solo only. About forty seconds after the player gets the HR service to answer, Maddison's voice comes over the walkie.",
		"action": "Over the walkie, unhurried and businesslike."},
	"l5_mimic_maddison_again": {"scene": "l5_radio", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Crew, it's Maddison. Still at the loading door. It's freezing down here.",
		"note": "Second time. Patient. She is never patient.",
		"cue": "Solo only. About fifty seconds later, if the player still hasn't opened the door or checked the badge log.",
		"action": "Over the walkie, steady, waiting."},
	"l5_mimic_maddison_last": {"scene": "l5_radio", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "You're leaving? I'm right here.",
		"note": "As the player leaves the floor. Quiet, flat, no breath.",
		"cue": "Solo only. Written for when the player leaves the floor without opening the door. Not heard in the game yet.",
		"action": "Over the walkie, very low."},
	"l5_ines_passed": {"scene": "l5_staffers", "speaker": "INES", "text": "That's a pass? Okay. Okay. I'm coming out. Don't talk to the one wearing my face.",
		"note": "Whispered. Relief and warning in the same breath.",
		"cue": "When the crew logs an escort pass for your badge. Your door may still be locked, or the crew may already have opened it.",
		"action": "Pressed against the door, then stepping out into the room."},
	"l5_tomas_passed": {"scene": "l5_staffers", "speaker": "TOMAS", "text": "Finally. I've been under this shelf since the lights went out. There's something at my desk, and it isn't me.",
		"note": "Annoyed first, scared underneath.",
		"cue": "When the crew logs an escort pass for your badge. Your door may still be locked, or the crew may already have opened it.",
